<span style="color:lightsteelblue">“Thanks!”</span> He says. <span style="color:lightsteelblue">“I don’t feel anything there because my mom takes this funny root thing and its juices makes my gums not hurt. Tastes kinda weird. Does your Dad do something like that when you lose a tooth?”</span> He then quickly changes the conversation slightly, saying he still has a lot of his baby teeth, stretching his mouth with his fingers, showing off his pearly whites. He lets go after a moment and complains that his mom wonders how he still has so many, even though he makes sure to take care of them. You think she is more surprised that, with all his dangerous climbing, it’s a miracle they haven’t been knocked out of him, but you wisely decide to keep it to yourself as your friend finds another story to start telling you. <br>
<<socialChange "Jackson" 3>>
